From 5b5515f69077402c4b816ddfaf4ae17c16a39c18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:45:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/194] media: i2c: Add OV02B10 24 MHz RAW10 bring-up driver

Adapt the GPL Rockchip 1600x1200 register sequence and controls to the
current V4L2 state/stream API. Use the MediaTek reference driver's timing
units: 16.5 MHz internal clock, 448 internal clocks per line and 66 Mpixel/s
MIPI rate. Express HBLANK in output pixels and VBLANK relative to 1200
active lines, preserving the register's 1220-line base and even VTS.

Retain the full 0x002b ID and 24 MHz clock guards. Separate analogue and
digital gain, update Bayer order with flips and hold the MIPI gate off
until controls are applied. Use SMBus byte operations with first-error
propagation. Power sequencing follows the decoded slot-2 module order;
failed clock enable reasserts reset and unwinds both supplies.

Sources:
- rockchip-linux/kernel, 99d20d8faae8ad9531f7c9244efe0fa3bce9d43b
- OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_mt6893, 48f1797695e24d46986a7c87dd91dd21cbf8c342
  drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/common/v1_1/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
  and drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/inc/kd_imgsensor.h

Rockchip source: https://github.com/rockchip-linux/kernel/blob/99d20d8faae8ad9531f7c9244efe0fa3bce9d43b/drivers/media/i2c/ov02b10.c

The public reference mode differs from Lenovo stock tuning and has not
been hardware tested. ARM64 W=1 object build, binding example and actual-C
mocked I2C/power/control checks pass, including all127 startup I2C failure
positions. These checks do not establish working capture or image quality.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@localhost>
